  text: Cypress, California, United States
  [button] Apply
  text: At Senra Systems, we believe that the future of manufacturing lies not in automation, but in configuration.
  text: We supercharge electrical wire harness manufacturing through software configuration, transforming skilled assembly tasks into high-throughpu
  text: We’re building a dedicated Production Engineering function at Senra Systems – a team that owns the floor, not the desk. As a Production Engi
  text: You’ll troubleshoot builds in real time, support first articles, verify cable and component kits, disposition non-conformances, and serve as
  text: Floor Troubleshooting & Real-Time Support
  text: Serve as the on-floor technical resource during active production – resolving assembly issues, documentation discrepancies, and build questi
  text: Identify and escalate systemic issues to the Lead PE or ME team with clear, structured documentation
  text: Participate in root cause analysis and corrective action implementation for recurring production issues
  text: Review and disposition non-conformances generated on the floor with documented rationale (use-as-is, rework, or scrap)
  text: Maintain NCR aging within SLA; escalate items that require engineering disposition beyond your scope
  text: Coordinate with Quality on in-process inspection holds and final disposition sign-off
  text: First Article & First Build Support
  text: Provide hands-on engineering support during first articles and new part number introductions
  text: Walk the floor during first builds, verify documentation accuracy, and identify gaps before they become production issues
  text: Capture redlines and documentation feedback and submit to the ME team in a structured, timely manner
  text: Kit Verification & Material Flow
  text: Audit incoming cable and component kits against the build package before they reach the floor
  text: Flag shortages, substitutions, or discrepancies and coordinate resolution with kitting, supply chain and engineering
  text: Technician Support & Mentorship
  text: Answer technical questions from assembly technicians on wire prep, crimping, connector insertion, splicing, and harness routing
  text: Coach to IPC/WHMA-A-620 and NASA 8739.4 workmanship standards; recognize and address non-conforming work at the source
  text: Contribute to a culture of quality ownership on the floor – every technician should know what good looks like
  text: What you'll bring to the team:
  text: 1–3 years of hands-on experience in wire harness or cable assembly manufacturing
  text: Working knowledge of wire harness assembly processes: wire prep, crimping, soldering, connector insertion, and harness routing
  text: Familiarity with IPC/WHMA-A-620 workmanship standards
  text: Ability to read and interpret wiring diagrams, schematics, assembly drawings, and work instructions
  text: Strong attention to detail and a quality-first mindset
  text: Must be a U.S. Person (U.S. Citizen or Lawful Permanent Resident)
  text: Prior experience as a manufacturing, build or sustaining engineer
  text: Extensive technical authoring experience i.e. developing engineering masters, dispositioning non conformances, etc.
  text: High degree of ownership, self-starting and proactive with a bias toward action and solutions
  text: Experience in an aerospace or defense manufacturing environment
  text: Exposure to NASA 8739.4 workmanship requirements
  text: Familiarity with MIL-spec connectors and contacts (D-sub, LEMO, Glenair, Amphenol, etc.)
  text: IPC/WHMA-A-620 CIS or CIT certification
  text: Experience with NCR or nonconformance management workflows
  text: Success in This Role Looks Like:
  text: Within 3–6 months, you will have:
  text: Become a trusted technical resource on the floor – technicians know to come to you first
  text: Achieved consistent NCR disposition turnaround within SLA with clear, documented rationale
  text: Supported at least one full first article cycle from kit verification through build completion and redline capture
  text: Demonstrated a consistent quality-first approach that has visibly reduced rework or build stops on your assigned product families
  text: Compensation will be based on experience, qualifications, and other job-related factors.
  text: This is an onsite role at our factory in Cypress, CA.
  text: Unmatched opportunities to drive impact on a friendly and mission-driven team
  text: Own a piece of the pie with equity participation!
  text: Comprehensive medical, dental, vision, life and long-term disability coverage
  text: Flexible Spending Account (FSA) and Dependent Spending Account (DSA) for health-related expenses
  text: 20 vacation days per year and 12 company holidays for rest and relaxation
  text: a 401(k) plan to set yourself up for retirement
  text: Choose a record you love, and we’ll add it to our growing vinyl collection!
  text: $50/month DoorDash credit – lunch is on us!
  text: Up to $100/month reimbursement for gym memberships
  text: Fully stocked kitchen with snacks and beverages
  text: Regular team-building events, lunches, and the occasional breakfast burrito!
  text: Bright, open office with communal spaces for collaboration and free parking
  text: Conveniently located near the metro, major freeways and local dining spots
  text: Interested in building your career at Senra Systems? Get future opportunities sent straight to your email.
